From 32736e24bfbee9865ddaaaa7f7db9c359934afff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sfxnz <sfxnz@spark1.tail1a9513.ts.net>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:40:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] inkling2: group-64 FP8 attention/gate/wr weights and
 qmmf_group dense projection fusion

Commit 4 (Lever 6 + Lever 10, zero extra VRAM):
- Add tf_qmmf_group_fp8g and tf_qmmf_group_fp8g_c entries in qmmf.cu and .fp8g support
  in qmmf_group.zig (with updated unit tests).
- Upgrade ATTN_FP8 / GATE_FP8 (and opt-in TF_INKLING2_WR_FP8=1, default 0) from single
  global power-of-2 scale to group-64 FP8 (.fp8g via tf_ink2_draft_pack_layers, gated by
  TF_INKLING2_ATTN_FP8_GROUP=1 default; 0 reverts to single-scale .fp8 for A/B). Fits
  within existing weight arena (1.0625 B/weight vs 2 B/weight BF16), zero extra VRAM.
- Fuse same-input dense attention projections at M <= 16 via cuda.qmmf_group.Group
  (TF_INKLING2_QMMF_GROUP=1 default): (wq, wk, wv, gate) on non-message sliding visits
  and (wq, gate[, wr]) on global/message visits, cutting 88-116 launches/round and
  sharing u_q loads across projections.
- Distinguish .fp8g vs .fp8 vs .bf16 in loop_backend.zig warmCacheKey.
